r1_repo/
anrf-aise-hack-2-0-round-2-sar-crop-health-yield-estimation/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# collected ground truth carries personal land-record data (7/12 owner names)
data_aux/ground_truth_vf12.csv

# live credentials - never commit
data_aux/.kdss_token
data_aux/*token*
.env

# staged upload artefacts are regenerable from src/make_upload_package.py
upload/

# regenerable pipeline output. results/cache/*.tif (172 MB) is rebuilt by prep_r2.py
# from the SLCs and is separately packaged into upload/kaggle_dataset/results/cache/
# for the Kaggle dataset -- tracking it here duplicated 172 MB of raster binaries in
# git for no reader who could not instead get them from that dataset or a rerun.
# results/figures/*.png is rebuilt by i10_media.py; docs/figures/ is the tracked,
# curated copy actually needed to render the shipped documents (see
# build_documents.py's sync_docs_figures()), so this copy is redundant with it.
results/cache/
results/figures/

# post-r2 experiment scratch. All regenerable by post-r2/experiments/*.py:
#  - e3's download/ is 41 MB of a COMPETITOR's published kernel output (rasters,
#    parquet, figures). Their work, not ours, and re-fetchable with the Kaggle CLI.
#    The derived comparison we actually cite (crop_agreement.csv) is kept.
#  - e1's stage/ is a full parallel rebuild of the submission under the corrected
#    calibration. Regenerable, and must never be mistaken for the shipped file.
post-r2/results/e3_consensus/download/
post-r2/results/e1_calibration/stage/

# The five competitors' Round 2 deliverables, kept locally as read-only analysis inputs.
# 22 MB of other teams' notebooks, reports and figures. They are published work, but
# redistributing them from our public repo is the team's call, not a default -- and the
# experiments name their source so anyone can re-obtain them. Flip this line if the team
# decides to vendor them.
post-r2/writeups_submissions/

# raw paged API responses, regenerable from data.gov.in with e10
post-r2/results/e10_kharif_anchors/vad_*.json
